      "side": 1,
      "message": "This sentence is a little confusing, because actually it doesn\u0027t happen \"often\". Apps don\u0027t generally have this problem. So, my question is:\nWill this run on code outside of the system_server? \n\nIf not really, then I\u0027d recommend rewording to\n\n\n\n```suggestion\n      Calling `PendingIntent.getActivity()` in the `system_server` often accidentally uses the user 0 context.  Since there\u0027s no explicit user parameter in the `getActivity` method, it can be hard to tell at a glance which user the `PendingIntent` activity is associated with, making the code less readable.\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 86,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 115
      },
      "revId": "d0ce8aad4bfd8da2cdb92c62bfa5642dc006dc0b",
